# EVERY SPELLING OF A CONTAINER CONSTRUCTION REACHES `create`'S `capacity`: the
# argument after the parenthesised type, labelled or -- as the first unlabelled
# argument, which binds the first declared parameter -- unlabelled; a
# `capacity:` inside the type application; the bare application; a value
# computed at run time. Each capacity printed is the one asked for.
main: function is {
    a: (ListVal t: i64) capacity: 8
    b: (ListVal t: i64 capacity: 10)
    c: ListVal u32 capacity: 12
    n: 16.u64
    d: (ListVal t: i64) capacity: n
    e: (ListVal t: i64) capacity: n * 2
    f: (MapVV k: i64 v: i64) capacity: 8
    g: (SetVal k: i64) capacity: 4
    h: (MapRV K: String v: i64) capacity: 4
    i: IdSet u64 capacity: 64
    print "lists: \{a.capacity} \{b.capacity} \{c.capacity} \{d.capacity} \{e.capacity}"
    print "others: \{f.length} \{g.length} \{h.length} \{i.length}"
}
